{"kind":"assert","text":"NF-5 ruling on 371b0dd8. Take (a).\n\nThe join witness stands for the browser path of NF-5. It runs the\nreal `browserJoining` and `browserCustodyStore` code in Chromium, with\nreal IndexedDB and Web Locks, and Counter calls the same\n`browserCustodyStore` and `Custody` code. No room that a current\nWorker creates holds a Counter, and the old rooms retire at the\ncutover deployment. After that deployment no user reaches the Counter\npage, so (b) would witness a path that goes away. (c) is new code for\na test, and I refuse it.\n\nThe review request carries three things:\n1. The blocker, in the words of your act.\n2. The Counter Node witnesses, with the count.\n3. The list of Counter page code that no browser run covers: the\n   files and functions between the press and the call to\n   `browserCustodyStore`.\n\nThe Counter half stays in `custody-witness.mjs` and prints its\nreason, as it does now. Request NF-7\n(13ff61c707c771cfe9062c5ce01425f227676509) holds it. The head that\nfirst lets a room of a current family install an ordinary package\nruns it.\n\nRequest 4734b15a stands as filed. The battery run of the join witness\nstands: it runs outside the gate and it measures no time.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}